// Allocation-attribution fixture (attribution category, D-385/D-386): the
// dispatch-equivalent, growth-free control for attr-build.grob — the dedicated
// fixture phase 1 §4 named as missing ("this note has not isolated it with its
// own dedicated fixture").
//
// xs.contains(i) and xs.append(i) are bound by the same OpCode.GetProperty path
// through ArrayNatives.GetMethod, both as `new NativeFunction(name, 1, ...)`
// capturing the receiver and ignoring the VmInvoker — so both pay the identical
// per-call NativeFunction/delegate/display-class triple. The array stays empty,
// so contains scans nothing and the backing GrobArray never grows.
//
// attr-build minus attr-array-dispatch therefore isolates array growth alone;
// attr-build minus attr-native does not, because attr-native runs the
// structurally cheaper Stdlib-plugin path (registered once, GetGlobal per call).
xs: int[] := []
for i in 1..1000 {
    xs.contains(i)
}
